# Project — Claude Instructions

## Generated Documents

When producing any structured output — audits, reviews, implementation
plans, phase summaries, spec analyses, or similar — write it as an HTML
file to `.claude/` and display only a brief summary in chat.

**Workflow:**
1. Write the document to `.claude/<name>-<date>.html`
2. Read the live port: `PORT=$(cat .claude/server.port 2>/dev/null || echo 7432)`
   Update the `Alt+D` keybinding in the IDE's user keybindings file to
   `http://localhost:${PORT}/<name>-<date>.html`
3. The doc server auto-starts when the project folder opens (via the
   `Start Claude doc server` task in `.vscode/tasks.json`). If not
   running, start manually: `python3 .claude/server.py &`
   It writes its bound port to `.claude/server.port` and auto-selects
   the next free port if the default (7432) is taken by another project.
4. Post a one-paragraph summary with a link to the file
5. Tell the user to press **Alt+D** to open it in the Simple Browser

Do not paste the full document content into the chat window.

**Every generated HTML document must include the annotation system** — JS-driven
`✎ Annotate` buttons on every `.finding`/`.card` div, every `h2`/`h3` heading,
and every table section header row (single `<td>` with `colspan > 1`). Notes
persist via a relative `/annotations/${DOC}` API call — the port never needs
to be hardcoded inside the document. See `templates/review-template.html` for
the full CSS + JS block to copy into every document.

## Project Context

- **Doc server:** served from `.claude/` on the port in `.claude/server.port`
- **Keybinding:** `Alt+D` opens latest doc in the IDE's Simple Browser
- **Spec docs:** All-caps `.md` files are the user's own design/arch/spec
  documents. Assist with formatting, presentation, and semantic
  completeness only — do not alter decisions.
- **Status updates:** Provide 1–12 word updates every 15–30 seconds
  during long-running tasks.
- **Chat formatting:** Write for a narrow panel — short paragraphs,
  no wall-to-wall prose.

